From 8067a79112edb968d4af1ab09810e9bcf9b4ec33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 07:43:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] A caption's ampersand marks a mnemonic, it is not text

WinForms marks the mnemonic of a caption with '&' and writes a literal
ampersand as '&&'; GTK marks it with '_' and writes a literal underscore
as '__'. Nothing converted between them, so a button whose Text was
"&Run" showed the ampersand instead of underlining the R, and Alt+R did
nothing.

Button, CheckBox, RadioButton, Label and GroupBox now convert the caption
on the way to the widget and turn the underline on afterwards, because
gtk_label_set_text clears the flag. Each keeps the caption as the
application wrote it, so Text still reads back "&Run": the widget holds
GTK's spelling, which reports the displayed text instead.

Label gains UseMnemonic, which WinForms has and this did not.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
